{"conjecture": "Software maintainability degrades because each locally correct change encodes tacit, undocumented assumptions held only by the developers who made it. As those developers rotate off the project, the knowledge that connects individual changes into a coherent mental model leaves with them. Later developers, lacking this tacit context, must treat existing code as a black box, making changes that are technically correct in isolation but incrementally diverge from the system's original architectural intent."}
